{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"consequence-theorems","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765","passage_ref":"sha256:f7c2487ba172be55e583becc143742c2d34c576d0d1339fd730197a0c97bb374/papers/long.md/sha256:57d520f131d63518eaab4bc49e02c1466414e4aa6afcee1b9cabfc26bbc1f419/papers/long.json/passages/consequence-theorems","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","span":{"end_byte":213560,"end_line":2401,"start_byte":190990,"start_line":2062},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c19&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.record-257bm-c19&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&node=long.record-257bm-c19&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c19&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=ac2deba6807718a1f836c82d6d89d9ab858a20e443b91d7f793c5fe9eb3ad765&ref=sha256%3A264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c%2Fnodes%2Flong.record-257bm-c19","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c19"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c19"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c19","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.87 (An eventual nonnegative margin suffices)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.87, p. 69, label record:257bm-c19","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Fix a positive depth $k$ and put $D=G\\cap\\{2,\\ldots,k\\}$. The following conditions are equivalent:\n$$\nr_k(1/2)<2^{-(k+1)}\n \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n F_k(J)\\ge0\\ \\text{for some }J\\ge0.\n$$\nHere $F_k(J)$ is the integer expression defined in Theorem 6.13. Its normalised value is\n$$\n2^{-J}F_k(J)=\\sum_{i=1}^{J}c_D(k+1+i)2^{-i}-C_D(k).\n$$\nThis normalised expression, not necessarily $F_k(J)$ itself, is nondecreasing in $J$. Its limit is $1-2^{k+1}r_k(1/2)$, by the finite-support Lambert identity. This is positive exactly under the strict dyadic inequality on the left. At positive $k$, oddness of the reduced excess numerator excludes equality at zero.*\n\n*The result supplies some finite horizon, not the horizon $J=c-3$ required in the crossing application. More quantitatively, write $\\eta=1-2^{k+1}r_k(1/2)>0$. Since $\\sum_{r\\ge1}c_D(m+r)2^{-r}\\le m+2$, the omitted tail shows that $(k+J+3)2^{-J}<\\eta$ suffices for $F_k(J)>0$. The value $\\eta$ is rational for the finite support $D$, so this is an effective sufficient test. Proving it at the prescribed horizon is a separate arithmetic obligation.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c19","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c19","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c19%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_coeffTail_le_index_add_two%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"